=== 8. RANKED GENE LISTS (GSEA prerank input) ===
GSEA RANKING METRIC (pre-specified, fixed before any enrichment was seen):
  metric = sign(shrunken log2FC) * |shrunken log2FC| * (-log10 RAW Wald p) == shrunken log2FC * (-log10 p)
  Rationale: the task filter already thresholds effect size and significance separately; the ranked
  list must still order genes by BOTH, otherwise a 2-gene-tall high-count pathway and a large-effect
  low-count pathway tie. A pure shrunken-log2FC ranking is written too, as a documented alternative,
  because the choice can change the top pathway.
  Handling: p==0 (float underflow) is floored to 1e-300 (-> -log10 p = 300) so no infinite weights;
  genes with NaN p or NaN SE are DROPPED from the ranked list; genes with baseMean < 1 are excluded.
  Ties are broken deterministically by (shrunken log2FC desc, geneID asc) so the seed/permutation
  result is reproducible. Duplicate symbols after mapping are collapsed by MEAN of the metric (an
  Ensembl->symbol many-to-one collapse); unmapped genes are dropped from enrichment but kept in the
  CSVs. Gene sets evaluated with min_size=15, max_size=500 (GSEApy defaults for KEGG).
